{"id":"s1.2.10","slug":"multiplying-two-numbers-equidistant-from-a-third-number","title":"Multiplying Two Numbers Equidistant from a Third Number","content":"<p class=\"mb-4\">This trick uses the difference of squares formula, $(x-d)(x+d) = x^2 - d^2$. It's useful for multiplying two numbers that are equally spaced from a convenient middle number (usually a multiple of 10 or 5).</p><p class=\"mb-4\"><strong>Procedure:</strong></p><ul class=\"list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 mb-4\"><li>Find the middle number between the two numbers being multiplied and square it.</li><li>Find the difference between the middle number and one of the original numbers, and square that difference.</li><li>Subtract the second result from the first.</li></ul><p>For example, $83 \\times 87$. The middle number is 85, and the distance is 2. The calculation is $85^2 - 2^2 = 7225 - 4 = 7221$.</p>","summary":"This trick uses the difference of squares formula, .","generation_guideline":"Generate a multiplication problem of two numbers that are equidistant from a multiple of 10 or 5.","questions":[{"id":1,"text":"Calculate $84 \\times 86$.","answer":"7224","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":2,"text":"Calculate $53 \\times 57$.","answer":"3021","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":3,"text":"Calculate $48 \\times 52$.","answer":"2496","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":4,"text":"Calculate $62 \\times 58$.","answer":"3596","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":5,"text":"Calculate $6.8 \\times 7.2$.","answer":"48.96","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":6,"text":"Calculate $88 \\times 82$.","answer":"7216","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":7,"text":"Calculate $36 \\times 24$.","answer":"864","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":8,"text":"Calculate $7.6 \\times 8.4$.","answer":"63.84","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":9,"text":"Calculate $5.3 \\times 4.7$.","answer":"24.91","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":10,"text":"Calculate $51 \\tim